  "review": "machine",
  "duration": 259.99675,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 6.92,
      "end": 17.08,
      "text": "I mourn the banners in the rain, the tavern doors, the carriage lane,",
      "uncertain": false
    },
    {
      "start": 17.26,
      "end": 27.3,
      "text": "when every fellow, proud and grand, could wear his fortune in his hand.",
      "uncertain": false
    },
    {
      "start": 27.3,
      "end": 32.78,
      "text": "The tailor sighed, the ladies knew",
      "uncertain": false
    },
    {
      "start": 32.78,
      "end": 37.58,
      "text": "What gossip through the market slew",
      "uncertain": true
    },
    {
      "start": 37.58,
      "end": 42.82,
      "text": "And horses bright with knowing eyes",
      "uncertain": false
    },
    {
      "start": 42.82,
      "end": 49.32,
      "text": "Would leave us all to theorize",
      "uncertain": false
    },
    {
      "start": 50.96,
      "end": 56.36,
      "text": "They went beyond the western hill",
      "uncertain": false
    },
    {
      "start": 56.36,
      "end": 60.8,
      "text": "With ancient patience, siren will",
      "uncertain": true
    },
    {
      "start": 60.8,
      "end": 65.88,
      "text": "No scholar ever wrote it down",
      "uncertain": true
    },
    {
      "start": 65.88,
      "end": 70.74,
      "text": "No bishop settled it in town",
      "uncertain": false
    },
    {
      "start": 70.74,
      "end": 74.82,
      "text": "Were they bound for fields of gold?",
      "uncertain": false
    },
    {
      "start": 75.34,
      "end": 79.78,
      "text": "Were they following tales untold?",
      "uncertain": false
    },
    {
      "start": 79.96,
      "end": 84.38,
      "text": "Their boofbeats answered, then were gone",
      "uncertain": false
    },
    {
      "start": 84.38,
      "end": 89.44,
      "text": "A riddle carried into dawn",
      "uncertain": true
    },
    {
      "start": 90.86,
      "end": 96.54,
      "text": "Oh, where are the days that made us stare",
      "uncertain": false
    },
    {
      "start": 96.54,
      "end": 101.66,
      "text": "The proud old man, the midnight air",
      "uncertain": false
    },
    {
      "start": 101.66,
      "end": 106.2,
      "text": "The horses going, none could say",
      "uncertain": false
    },
    {
      "start": 106.2,
      "end": 110.82,
      "text": "What secret pulls them far away",
      "uncertain": false
    },
    {
      "start": 110.82,
      "end": 115.92,
      "text": "Let solemn bells and lamplights sing",
      "uncertain": false
    },
    {
      "start": 115.92,
      "end": 122.04,
      "text": "We knew so little of everything",
      "uncertain": false
    },
    {
      "start": 126.82,
      "end": 132.32,
      "text": "Now polished clocks explain the sky",
      "uncertain": false
    },
    {
      "start": 132.32,
      "end": 137.08,
      "text": "And clever papers tell us why",
      "uncertain": false
    },
    {
      "start": 137.08,
      "end": 146.36,
      "text": "They measure thunder, charge the sea, and still cannot remember me.",
      "uncertain": false
    },
    {
      "start": 146.72,
      "end": 155.84,
      "text": "For all their certainty and flame, the oldest question stays the same.",
      "uncertain": false
    },
    {
      "start": 155.84,
      "end": 160.84,
      "text": "Why did the horses leave the gate?",
      "uncertain": false
    },
    {
      "start": 161.04,
      "end": 166.26,
      "text": "Why did desire arrive so late?",
      "uncertain": false
    },
    {
      "start": 168.12,
      "end": 173.64,
      "text": "I do not ask to turn the years",
      "uncertain": false
    },
    {
      "start": 173.64,
      "end": 178.78,
      "text": "Or trade our wisdom for our tears",
      "uncertain": true
    },
    {
      "start": 180.18,
      "end": 184.76,
      "text": "But let one shadow cross the square",
      "uncertain": false
    },
    {
      "start": 184.76,
      "end": 190.3,
      "text": "One laughing room or in the air",
      "uncertain": false
    },
    {
      "start": 190.3,
      "end": 195.88,
      "text": "Let one dark stallion raise his head",
      "uncertain": false
    },
    {
      "start": 195.88,
      "end": 202.96,
      "text": "And speak the things we never said",
      "uncertain": false
    },
    {
      "start": 204.5,
      "end": 210.42,
      "text": "Oh, bring me the days that made us stare",
      "uncertain": false
    },
    {
      "start": 210.42,
      "end": 215.34,
      "text": "The wild old jokes, the winter air",
      "uncertain": false
    },
    {
      "start": 215.34,
      "end": 220.16,
      "text": "The horses going grave and free",
      "uncertain": true
    },
    {
      "start": 220.16,
      "end": 224.42,
      "text": "Their mystery kept company",
      "uncertain": false
    },
    {
      "start": 224.42,
      "end": 230.36,
      "text": "Though every banner fades from view",
      "uncertain": false
    },
    {
      "start": 230.36,
      "end": 235.58,
      "text": "The unanswered road remains true",
      "uncertain": false
    },
    {
      "start": 235.58,
      "end": 248.14,
      "text": "I lift my voice where they have been, and bless the road they vanished in.",
      "uncertain": false
    }
  ]
}
